                            {
                                "example_id": "512ca9a5-74cd-4838-b644-a194fd189263",
                                "sense_id": "01b2e716-8ada-374a-9fc6-cf3f49ef4917",
                                "text": "[243] IV. THE MOON A WATER-DEITY. We design this chapter to be the completion of moon-worship, and at the same time an anticipation of those lunary superstitions which are but scattered leaves from luniolatry, the parent tree."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "810ad2e3-ccbe-423b-999b-5ef485867ee2",
                                "sense_id": "01b2e716-8ada-374a-9fc6-cf3f49ef4917",
                                "text": "He has moreover enriched his work by adding to it an ecclesiastic compute with all its indications; an orrery after the Copernican system, representing the mean tropical revolutions of each of the planets visible to the naked eye, the phases of the moon, the eclipses of the sun and moon, calculated for ever; the true time and the sideral time; a new celestial globe with the procession of the equinoxes, solar and lunary equations for the reduction of the mean geocentric ascension and declension of the sun and moon at true times and places."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53de1f32-399b-42d1-af07-f8df3b9d85bb",
                                "sense_id": "01b2e716-8ada-374a-9fc6-cf3f49ef4917",
                                "text": "This lunary sphere, lowest and basest to divine bodies, is first and highest to terrestrial bodies."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
